WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:09.790
China is already a giant.

00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:16.490
This country is the largest trading power
in the world

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:20.259
They lead the world with hundreds of products
and have one of the largest foreign currency

00:00:20.259 --> 00:00:21.930
reserves on the entire planet.

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:26.300
Not even the “petromonachies” in the Persian
Gulf can compete with this giant.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:31.070
And with all of this, it isn't surprising
to find some analysts who state that China

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:34.840
will pass the United States as the leading
economic power…

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:37.290
But with a lot more inhabitants!

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:42.710
However, we usually forget a very important
thing, and this is that GDP is not everything,

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:47.999
and economic power, the real power, is closely
related to corporate power and, when it comes

00:00:47.999 --> 00:00:52.570
to that, China is still far from reaching
the level of the United States.

00:00:52.570 --> 00:00:57.980
If we look at the top 100 largest companies
in the world, 56 are American, and only 11

00:00:57.980 --> 00:00:58.980
are Chinese.

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:02.899
And this is something to really bear in mind
because multinationals are in control of foreign

00:01:02.899 --> 00:01:05.950
investment and of 80% of the world’s exports.

00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:10.490
Now, the big question is what is going to
happen to these Chinese companies in the future?

00:01:10.490 --> 00:01:11.830
How are things changing?

00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:13.790
And what can we expect?

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:20.460
These are some of the questions we are going
to answer in today’s video!

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:23.150
The Chinese Giant’s Development

00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:28.540
The Chinese economy has had an impressive
growth rate in the last three decades, and

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:31.610
the key was the concept of: “The World’s
Factory”.

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:34.110
That is what China is known for.

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:39.280
They are known as a country that has become
a world power and has lifted hundreds of thousands

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:45.030
people from poverty with a relatively simple
premise: producing everything, and produce

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:47.650
it at a low cost.

00:01:47.650 --> 00:01:50.280
Toys, electronics, tools, clothing…

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:55.100
when you enter a store you are going to find
hundreds of products with something in common:

00:01:55.100 --> 00:02:01.490
they are all manufactured in massive industrial
areas located all over China.

00:02:01.490 --> 00:02:06.990
However, in order for a country to really
be the leading economic power, these companies

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:12.500
need to start producing much more complex
products, and they will have to stop competing

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:15.570
on cost and start looking for higher added
value.

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:20.579
This can include the production of things
like capital assets, planes, medical devices,

00:02:20.579 --> 00:02:37.599
and computer processors.

00:02:37.599 --> 00:02:42.090
And today, all these sectors are dominated
by the large multinationals of the United

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:47.530
States, South Korea, Europe, and Japan.

00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:54.799
It is true, that many leading products are
manufactured in China, like the iPhone for

00:02:54.799 --> 00:03:00.170
example, but… this is not exactly true,
because what China actually does is just the

00:03:00.170 --> 00:03:01.250
assembly.

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:04.922
What this means is that the more complex parts
are bought from other countries and then they

00:03:04.922 --> 00:03:07.180
are simply put together in China.

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:09.370
To better illustrate this consider that:

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:14.150
Each year, China imports more than 200 billion
dollars in semiconductors, which are essential

00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:16.790
in the manufacturing of mobile devices.

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:21.250
Just as a comparison, that is more money than
what the country spends on petrol!

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:25.459
However, Chinese companies have made many
advances…

00:03:25.459 --> 00:03:31.870
Today, a fourth of all exports are of capital
assets, such as machines, for example, or

00:03:31.870 --> 00:03:33.629
high tech products.

00:03:33.629 --> 00:03:39.609
In some sectors like telecommunications, wind
turbines, or high speed trains, Chinese companies

00:03:39.609 --> 00:03:41.980
are the world leaders.

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:49.400
And it is not just that, Chinese companies
are learning how to make it in the international

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:53.750
market.

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:55.519
The Great Chinese Conquest

00:03:55.519 --> 00:04:02.480
2016 was the 40th anniversary of the end of
the cultural revolution: this was a terrifying

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:08.120
campaign which Mao organized in order to purify
the revolution and finish off all remnants

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:10.219
of capitalism in Chinese society.

00:04:10.219 --> 00:04:13.290
Well, since then, things have changed a lot…

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:18.930
So much that China is only behind the United
States in terms of numbers of multinational

00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:19.980
companies.

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:23.880
Companies in this country are starting to
make it to global markets… and, well, they

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:25.680
are doing it really well!

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:33.360
In 2016, Chinese companies spent the amazing
amount of 225 billion dollars in the purchase

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:34.500
of foreign companies.

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:42.490
In Europe and the United States alone they
bought out more than 450 companies.

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:47.539
These Chinese companies are buying all kinds
of businesses: mining companies, banks, oil

00:04:47.539 --> 00:04:52.690
companies, pharmaceutical companies, agricultural
companies, even luxury hotel chains, jewelry

00:04:52.690 --> 00:04:54.960
companies and football clubs.

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:58.599
Yep, you heard it right, the Chinese, dear
viewer, have even bought Inter Milan, and

00:04:58.599 --> 00:05:01.050
that is just one example.

00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:05.460
“Manchester City gets $400 million Chinese
investment deal”

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:10.270
But, if there is one thing in particular that
the Chinese like to invest in, well that would

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:12.250
be developing countries.

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:18.919
Even though Australia and the United States
are the two main countries where the Chinese

00:05:18.919 --> 00:05:24.470
money is invested, more than half of all Chinese
investment is made in emerging countries in

00:05:24.470 --> 00:05:27.800
Asia, Africa, Latin America and the Middle
East.

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:32.949
So, we could almost say that, the more risky
the country, the more willing the Chinese

00:05:32.949 --> 00:05:34.370
are to invest.

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:38.740
Now this might surprise you, but this isn’t
the end of the story…

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:41.270
Chinese companies are also starting to compete
hard.

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:42.270
Want some proof of this?

00:05:42.270 --> 00:05:46.080
Well, if there was only one Chinese company
in the top 100 most valuable companies in

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:50.400
2006, there were 14 by the year 2015.

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:53.440
Take a look at the smartphone industry alone.

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:59.819
Up until recently, having a Chinese phone
was a bit…

00:05:59.819 --> 00:06:00.819
weird...

00:06:00.819 --> 00:06:01.819
right?

00:06:01.819 --> 00:06:06.080
Well, today, the four main Chinese manufacturers:
Oppo, Huawei, Vivo and Xiaomi aren't just

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:11.349
more famous than they were a few years ago,
they also take more than 10% of the world’s

00:06:11.349 --> 00:06:16.229
profits in this industry... and this is a
figure that is growing more and more every

00:06:16.229 --> 00:06:17.229
year.

00:06:17.229 --> 00:06:19.000
How about another example?

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:25.280
Lenovo, a Chinese multinational that was born
just a few years ago, bought the laptop division

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:31.110
of IBM, and is now the largest computer company
in the world, and they even supply equipment

00:06:31.110 --> 00:06:32.319
to the Pentagon!

00:06:32.319 --> 00:06:33.710
And want even more examples?

00:06:33.710 --> 00:06:37.690
There’s Haier, the biggest manufacturer
of household appliances; or Cofco, a company

00:06:37.690 --> 00:06:41.580
that’s acquiring land all over the world,
like sugar cane plantations in Australia,

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:43.889
French vineyards or soy plantations in Brazil.

00:06:43.889 --> 00:06:48.729
There is also Geely, a car company which became
of international note when it bought out Volvo

00:06:48.729 --> 00:06:49.770
in 2010.

00:06:49.770 --> 00:06:58.699
Yep, Volvo, that legendary Swedish car brand
is now property of the Chinese…

00:06:58.699 --> 00:07:05.700
But, if there is a sector where China is really
getting ahead, it is , against all odds, the

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:06.700
internet.

00:07:06.700 --> 00:07:11.020
And I say against all odds because, as you
all know, the Chinese net is subject to complete

00:07:11.020 --> 00:07:16.400
control and censorship by the Chinese government
with something known as “The Great Firewall”,

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:21.530
which blocks access to Facebook, Google, and
the Economist, to name just three.

00:07:21.530 --> 00:07:25.449
However, in China it’s pretty normal to
do everything through apps.

00:07:25.449 --> 00:07:29.520
For example, when you visit China you rarely
pay with credit cards, the most common thing

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:34.379
is to pay with a mobile phone using the app
Wechat - this is a “super-app” that is

00:07:34.379 --> 00:07:38.260
like an all-in-one: Facebook, Paypal, Gmail,
Twitter etc…

00:07:38.260 --> 00:07:45.200
By the way, Wechat is property of Tencent,
one of the top 15 most valuable companies

00:07:45.200 --> 00:07:49.680
in the world, which is also the world’s
largest supplier of online games, and one

00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:52.400
of the majority shareholders of Tesla.

00:07:52.400 --> 00:08:00.280
So, by now, you are probably realising that,
yep, the Chinese are everywhere.

00:08:00.280 --> 00:08:04.550
As for &nbsp;another example of their success,
consider Alibaba, an e-commerce company that

00:08:04.550 --> 00:08:08.380
brings in $450 billion every year.

00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:09.639
Not bad right?

00:08:09.639 --> 00:08:14.710
And in China alone they have 400 million clients.

00:08:14.710 --> 00:08:20.090
As Napoleon said:
“Let China sleep, for when she wakes she

00:08:20.090 --> 00:08:21.280
will shake the world”

00:08:21.280 --> 00:08:26.009
But before we all get scared, think about
what it all means: more competition, better

00:08:26.009 --> 00:08:30.020
prices, better products, and faster technological
development…

00:08:30.020 --> 00:08:33.479
As consumers we can benefit a great deal from
this transition.

00:08:33.479 --> 00:08:38.600
Now, it obviously has plenty of risks too…or
at least this is what US intelligence agencies

00:08:38.600 --> 00:08:40.300
are warning.

00:08:40.300 --> 00:08:45.570
“According to the House Permanent Select
Committee on Intelligence’s report, Chinese

00:08:45.570 --> 00:08:51.260
companies cannot be trusted to be free of
foreign state influence and thus pose a security

00:08:51.260 --> 00:08:53.990
threat to the United States and to our systems”

00:08:53.990 --> 00:08:56.870
And then there is the risk for companies,
they will have even much more competition…

00:08:56.870 --> 00:09:02.130
although many more opportunities too, which
we previously discussed in the video we are

00:09:02.130 --> 00:09:03.370
linking to on the screen now!

00:09:03.370 --> 00:09:05.950
But, let’s not get too ahead of ourselves…

00:09:05.950 --> 00:09:11.430
Chinese companies are still far behind in
technological terms, and they are in debt,

00:09:11.430 --> 00:09:15.320
and a lot of it…

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:20.070
“China's corporate debt levels are too high
but it will take time to bring them down to

00:09:20.070 --> 00:09:23.160
more manageable levels” Zhou Xiaochuan,
Head of the Central Bank of China.

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:27.840
And that is not the end of it, don’t forget
that China is a dictatorship, and this means

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:31.230
that the government has too much power when
it comes to corporate decisions.

00:09:31.230 --> 00:09:34.940
Further the government is rather arbitrary
and unpredictable.

00:09:34.940 --> 00:09:39.040
For example, a few years ago the government
&nbsp;encouraged Chinese companies to try the

00:09:39.040 --> 00:09:43.230
international market and they would loan them
as much money as they needed to do so, but

00:09:43.230 --> 00:09:45.040
now they have decided they want the opposite…

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:50.730
If a Chinese company wants to buy out a foreign
company, they need the approval of the Chinese

00:09:50.730 --> 00:09:54.870
Communist Party and there are new tough limitations
on money leaving the country.

00:09:54.870 --> 00:09:59.130
Further to that we have to add censorship,
legal uncertainty, trade obstacles, the bad

00:09:59.130 --> 00:10:02.800
reputation of Chinese products… and so on
and so forth.

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:08.970
So, we can say that right now the United States’
position as leader is not in particular danger,

00:10:08.970 --> 00:10:13.130
unless something changes that is more dramatic
than what we are currently seeing.

00:10:13.130 --> 00:10:14.220
Long term though…

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:15.220
well who knows…

00:10:15.220 --> 00:10:19.971
So I really hope you enjoyed this video, please
hit like if you did, and don’t forget to

00:10:19.971 --> 00:10:23.290
subscribe if you haven’t already, brand
new videos every Monday and Thursday.

00:10:23.290 --> 00:10:27.480
And don’t forget to check out the Reconsider
Media podcasts - they provided the vocals

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:29.720
in this episode that aren’t mine.

00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:31.640
And as always, I’ll see you in the next
video.

